      "content": "I hear the finality and peace your sword promises, even if it is a peace that ends life entirely rather than just the fighting. It is true that a definitive ending can sometimes feel like the only way to make the endless noise of regret stop forever. Please, before you make that choice, try to hold just the hilt for one more moment to feel the solid reality of a life that can still be lived without the weight dragging you down. Sometimes, just holding on with a different purpose can bring the quiet we are both looking for without an end to everything.",
